00:14:46.000 --> 00:15:27.000
Sing Chong became a bustling department store, Hawking Asian Art, which it still is to this day. But nonetheless, the designers that looked 10 Eli hired created a striking building. And other merchants rebuilding in Chinatown couldn't help but notice. Soon, Sing Chang's bombastic Shinwazari look had become the style for most new structures going up in Chinatown. The architects who were trying to reproduce Beijing in San Francisco may have gotten a lot of the details wrong. But for the Taurus, they were wrong in all the right ways. Taurus loved the new Chinatown. This was exactly the westerner friendly version of China they wanted,
兴昌变成了繁华的百货公司，叫卖亚洲艺术品，至今仍然如此。尽管如此，陆廷礼雇用的设计者还是创造了一座引人注目的建筑。其他在唐人街重建的商家也注意到了这一点。很快，兴昌那浮夸的“中国风”外观成为了唐人街大多数新建筑的风格。那些试图在旧金山复制北京的建筑师可能把很多细节都搞错了。但对游客来说，他们在所有正确的地方都错了。游客喜欢新的唐人街。这正是他们想要的西方人友好的中国版本，

29
00:15:27.000 --> 00:16:05.000
vaguely exotic, but safe enough for a middle-class white America. The visitors began to flow into Chinatown, and so did their cash. In Chinatown's pleasant new appearance was beginning to change popular sentiment towards the Chinese people. American newspapers made it explicit that the neighborhood makeover was causing them to rethink their contempt for the Chinese. As one newspaper, the bulletin put it in 1909, quote, China Town is one of the most noted places on the American continent. We have held up to the public gaze for too long the racial grief that separates the yellow and white people of the earth."
隐约带有异国情调，但对中产阶级白人美国人来说足够安全。游客开始涌入唐人街，他们的现金也随之而来。唐人街崭新宜人的外表开始改变大众对中国人的看法。美国报纸明确表示，社区大改造让他们重新审视对中国人的蔑视。正如《公报》（The Bulletin）1909年所言，引述：“唐人街是美洲大陆最著名的地点之一。我们把隔离地球上黄种人和白人的种族悲剧在公众目光下展示得太久了。”

30
00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:38.000
And quote, Looktan Eli's plan had worked. And Chinese communities elsewhere in the US were taking note. All of the success of Chinatowns that have come in America take a cue from this, take a page from this playbook, New York San Francisco LA, Honolulu. They all sort of have their roots in San Francisco. That's Bonnie Saw again. She says the visual style and tourist-friendly attitude that San Francisco's Chinatown had perfected soon began to spread.
引述完毕。陆廷礼的计划成功了。美国其他地方的华人社区也注意到了这一点。美国所有取得成功的唐人街都从中吸取了经验，从这套剧本中借鉴了一页，纽约、旧金山、洛杉矶、檀香山。它们的根源都或多或少可以追溯到旧金山。又是邦妮·索伊。她说旧金山唐人街完善的视觉风格和对游客友好的态度很快开始传播开来。

31
00:16:38.000 --> 00:17:24.000
In fact, the new Chinatown brand was so successful that it's still influencing Chinatowns being built in our own time. For instance, take the Chinatown in Las Vegas, which was created in the 90s. It also had the same pagoda ruflines and dragon gates, like the same language, the architectural language, the same architectural vernacular was being used to create the newest Chinatown that was used to create the oldest Chinatown. You know, you outsmarted the devil. You know, basically there is a phrase, you know, that they called white people, Bacquay, which is the white devil. I think that it was a victory, absolutely. Of course, this architectural revenge didn't instantly fix everything for the Chinese and San Francisco.
事实上，新的唐人街品牌是如此成功，以至于它至今仍在影响着正在建造的唐人街。例如，以拉斯维加斯的唐人街为例，它建于90年代。它也有相同的宝塔屋顶线条和龙门，就像同样的语言，建筑语言，同样的建筑白话被用来建造最新的唐人街，而这正是用来建造最古老的唐人街的。你知道，你智胜了恶魔。你知道，基本上有一个短语，你知道，他们叫白人“Bacquay”，也就是白鬼。我认为这绝对是一场胜利。当然，这种建筑上的复仇并没有立刻解决旧金山华人的所有问题。

32
00:17:24.000 --> 00:18:04.000
They still faced plenty of legal and popular discrimination. For example, they were still required by real estate laws to live in Chinatown. And on a federal level, the Chinese Exclusion Act itself wouldn't even be repealed until 1943. More than 30 years later. And even if the rebranding of Chinatown helped to ease negative sentiment towards the Chinese, Philip Choi believes it may also have helped promote certain stereotypes. It continues to provoke our fullness, and I remember my daughter coming home one day very annoyed and upset. Is it these people?
他们仍然面临着大量的法律和大众歧视。例如，房地产法律仍然要求他们住在唐人街。而在联邦层面，排华法案本身直到1943年才被废除。三十多年后。即使唐人街的重新包装有助于缓解对中国人的负面情绪，菲利普·崔（Philip Choi）认为它可能也助长了某些刻板印象。“它继续挑起我们的异国情调，我记得我女儿有一天回家时非常恼火和沮丧。她说这些人，

